  "task": "X54 h=4 shell-surplus norm-gate bridge",
  "theorem": "For every nonzero pair-sum shell S_s of size m_s, each unordered choice of two distinct shell pairs gives a nonzero h=2 pair-sum collision.  Distinct pairs in one shell are automatically disjoint, and by X41 each such collision is non-Phi-descended and p-norm-gated. Therefore the h=2 norm-gate surplus in centered shells is exactly sum_{s != 0} C(m_s,2).  By X48/X52, m_s is constant on H-cosets, so this equals n * sum_C C(m_C,2)."
